# Build context for the Trusted Server appliance image.
#
# Sizes below were measured with `du -sm` at the worktree root, not guessed.
# `target` is 141 MB and dominates everything else; `crates` is 10 MB and
# `docs` is 5 MB. Nothing outside `target` exceeds 1 MB.

# Rust build output, at the root and in any crate.
/target
**/target/

# Node dependencies. The image installs these itself in the builder stage.
**/node_modules/

# Git metadata. In a worktree `.git` is a small pointer file rather than an
# object store, so this saves little space, but neither build script reads git
# metadata so it has no business in the context either.
.git
.gitignore
.github/

# Agent and editor state. Everything under .claude is excluded except the
# directory holding this image's own entry point, which the Dockerfile COPYs.
# Written as "exclude the children, then whitelist" to mirror the repository's
# own .gitignore, rather than relying on re-including a child of an excluded
# directory.
.claude/*
!.claude/docker
.specstory/
.vscode/
.idea/

# EdgeZero local emulator state. Stale local config here would only confuse a
# reader of the image; nothing in the container reads it.
.edgezero/

# Operator secrets and local configuration. The appliance takes its config from
# a mounted file at run time, so none of this may be baked into a layer.
.env
.env.*
trusted-server.toml
js-assets.toml
*.pem
*.key

# Test and report output.
/benchmark-results/
/guest-profiles/
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
**/.browser-test-state.json

# Local tool downloads.
/spin
/spin.sig

# Editor backups and OS clutter.
**/*.rs.bk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Documentation and long-form markdown. The build does not read any of it.
docs/
CHANGELOG.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
FAQ_POC.md
ProjectGovernance.md
TESTING.md

# Deliberately NOT excluded: crates/trusted-server-js/dist.
# `crates/trusted-server-js/build.rs` asserts at line 112 that it found at
# least one `tsjs-*.js` bundle, and the directory is gitignored so it is absent
# from a clean checkout. Keeping it in the context leaves a Node-free build
# possible (prebuild `dist` on the host, then set TSJS_SKIP_BUILD=1) for the day
# the npm registry is unreachable. It is a few hundred KB at most.
